    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$210.22$ every 6 months.",
      "worked": "There are $21\\times2=42$ six-monthly periods, with interest of $9\\%\\div2=4.5\\%$ per period. The future value table gives a factor of $118.9248$.\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\text{table factor}\\times M\\\\25\\,000&=118.9248\\times M\\\\M&=\\frac{25\\,000}{118.9248}\\\\M&\\approx\\$210.22\\end{align*}$$\nThey need to deposit $\\$210.22$ every 6 months.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
